<title>SWEDEN: Trelleborg says Q1 profit falls 16 pct.</title>
<headline>Trelleborg says Q1 profit falls 16 pct.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1997-04-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Swedish mining and rubber group Trelleborg on Friday presented these earnings for the first three months of the year, ending March 31.</p>
<p>					(million crowns unless stated)</p>
<p> Profit after fin items		 300    vs 356</p>
<p> Sales					5,441  vs 5,163</p>
<p> Earnings per share (crowns)	  1.80   vs 2.15</p>
<p> Costs of goods sold		   4,486   vs 4,286</p>
<p> Costs for admin, sales, R&amp;D	   698   vs   598</p>
<p> Associated interests		     34   vs    32</p>
<p> Operating profit			  309   vs   294</p>
<p> Interest net			 CHARGE 9   vs    62 CREDIT</p>
<p> Taxes					  89   vs   102</p>
<p> Minorities				    0   vs     0</p>
<p> Net profit				  211   vs   254</p>
<p>NOTE -- A Reuter poll found analysts expected a profit after financial items of 317 million crowns.</p>
<p>-- Stockholm newsroom +46-8-700-1017</p>
</text>
